 "くったく": "قَلِقَ (To be troubled; to give way to mental anxiety or doubt.) / قَلَق (A strong feeling of anxiety.)  [worry] / مَلَل, ضَجَر (The state of being bored.)  [boredom]",
 "くったくた": "اِسْتَهْلَكَ, اِسْتَنْفَدَ (To use up; to deplete, drain or expend wholly, or use until the supply comes to )  [exhausted]\nمثال: もう朝から晩まで働いてクタクタだよ。\n→ I'm beat. I've been working from dawn to dusk. / [battered (esp. of clothing) ; worn out]\nمثال: 彼はくたくたの背広を着ていた。\n→ He was wearing a threadbare suit. / [(boiling) to a pulp ; to a mash]\nمثال: くたくたに煮る。\n→ Reduce to pulp by boiling.",
 "くったくない": "مُرْتَاحُ اَلْبَالِ, خَالِي اَلْقَلْبِ (Without cares or worries; free of concern or worries; without difficulty.)  [carefree]\noften 屈託なく",
 "くったくのない": "مُرْتَاحُ اَلْبَالِ, خَالِي اَلْقَلْبِ (Without cares or worries; free of concern or worries; without difficulty.)  [carefree]",
