 "くってかかる": "شَغَّلَ (To power up, to put into operation, to start, to activate (an appliance, light, ) / اِنْقَلَبَ عَلَى (To rebel against; to suddenly attack.)  [to turn on]\nمثال: あの野暮ったい服を幾らで買ったのかと聞いただけで、彼女は逆上して私にくってかかってきた。\n→ I only asked her what she paid for that dull-looking dress and she flew off the handle at me.",
 "くっと": "عَنْ غَيْرِ قَصْدٍ, بِدُونِ قَصْدٍ (Unintentionally; because of an oversight.)  [inadvertently (letting out a laugh)] / بِسُرْعَة, عَاجِلًا (Rapidly; with speed; fast; with expedition.)  [quickly]",
