 "これ": "هَٰذَا, هَٰذِهِ (The known (thing) (used in indicating something or someone about to be mentioned) / هَٰذَا, هَٰذِهِ (Designates the current or next instance.) / هٰذَا, هٰذِهِ (The thing, item, etc. being indicated.)  [this]\nindicating an item near the speaker, the action of the speaker, or the current topic\nمثال: これは面白い本だよ。\n→ This is an interesting book. / [this person]\nusu. indicating someone in one's in-group\nمثال: これは兄です。かっこいいですね。\n→ This is my brother. Handsome, isn't he? / الْآنَ, حَالًا (At the present time.) / بِمَا أَنّ, أَمَا وَأَنّ (Since, because, in light of the fact.)  [now]\nas これから, これまで, etc.\nمثال: 私はこれからは英語を一生懸命勉強します。\n→ I will study English hard from now on. / إِلَى هُنَا (To this place; used in place of the literary or archaic hither.)  [here]",
